---
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
import { siteConfig } from '../config/site';
---

<LegalLayout
  title="Website privacy policy"
  description="How the US5 Incorporation website handles information and enquiries."
  path="/privacy/"
  updated="28 August 2026"
  ><h2>Scope</h2><p>
    This policy covers this corporate website. Future mobile products will have separate policies
    based on their actual behavior.
  </p><h2>Information you choose to provide</h2><p>
    This website does not receive or store form submissions. The enquiry form prepares a message in
    your own email application. If you send it, US5 Incorporation receives the information through
    email and uses it to respond and manage the resulting correspondence.
  </p><h2>Website operation</h2><p>
    We do not intentionally deploy analytics, advertising, accounts, or non-essential cookies.
    GitHub Pages delivers the website and may process ordinary technical information such as IP
    addresses and request logs under GitHub’s own terms and privacy practices.
  </p><h2>Sharing and retention</h2><p>
    We do not sell website enquiry information. Email providers and infrastructure providers process
    information as needed to deliver their services. Correspondence may be retained while relevant
    to the enquiry, support, security, or legitimate record-keeping needs, then removed when no
    longer reasonably needed.
  </p><h2>Your choices</h2><p>
    You may contact us to ask about, correct, or request deletion of information held in
    correspondence, subject to information we reasonably need to retain for security, legal, or
    record-keeping purposes.
  </p><h2>Security</h2><p>
    We use reasonable care when handling correspondence, but no internet transmission or storage
    method can be guaranteed completely secure.
  </p><h2>Changes and contact</h2><p>
    We may update this policy when the website’s behavior changes. Questions can be sent to <a
      href={`mailto:${siteConfig.email}`}>{siteConfig.email}</a
    >.
  </p></LegalLayout
>
